      "text": "Hello, I'm Tom Vaughn, Principal Engineer at the Common Crawl Foundation. I'll be speaking about why open data is essential for open models. Most of today's foundational AI models would not exist without open web data, but very few talk about the data that makes them possible. So what is Common Crawl? Common Crawl is a 501c3 non-profit organization that's been archiving the web since 2007. We've built a corpus of over 300 billion web pages. That's more than 10 petabytes of data. It's all free, open, and hosted on AWS S3 through their open web data sponsorship program. It's also heavily used. More than 10,000 research papers cite Common Crawl's data.",
