      "text": "Every month we add between three and four billion new web pages to our archive. Our releases also include web graphs following each monthly crawl, from which we derive host-level and domain-level rankings, which steer our future crawls. We use harmonic centrality as a primary ranking algorithm, which is similar to page rank, but it's inherently harder to manipulate. This gives us a reliable way of seeing how well connected a host or domain is, allowing us to build a stratified sample of the web. This is harmonic centrality. In simple terms, the harmonic centrality of a vertex in a network measures how close that point is to all others. To find it, you look at every other point in the network,",
