      "text": "measure the distance to each one, and then take the sum of the inverses of those distances. This means that points closer to many others have a higher harmonic centrality, while those further away from others have a lower one. You can see these rankings and compare them with page rank, and search through them on our website. At the domain level, we can search for Wikipedia here, and we'll see that it has a page rank position of 34 and a harmonic centrality position of 15. At the host level, we can search for Wikipedia, and we'll see the page rank and harmonic centrality positions for those hosts within that domain. So why is common crawl important? This is a cumulative plot of common crawl citations",
