      "text": "in Google Scholar until January of 2025. You can see when the transformer paper was released in June of 2017. You can see when OpenAI released GPT-2 in February of 2019, and when big science bloom was released in July of 2022. For comparison, the Hubble Space Telescope is cited in a thousand papers per year. Common crawl is the backbone of modern AI. Over 80% of GPT-3's training tokens came from common crawl data. foundational data sets like Oscar, MC4, and the pile all rely on common crawl. So whenever you hear about a breakthrough in AI, the chances are it was fueled by open web data. There's a problem, however, with multi-lingual data. Our crawls contain much less content",
