      "text": "in languages other than English. In fact, you can see that around 45% of the data was identified as English in our most recent crawl. The next biggest language represented is Russian with about 6% and then German with around 5.8%. The large trance you can see labeled other represents a long tail of low resource languages. That imbalance leads to risks. Research shows models often behave unsafely in low resource languages. GPT-PALN-2, LAMA-2, and VIKUNA give unsafe responses for queries in languages other than English. Imagine selling a car where the brakes and the seatbelts only work in English-speaking countries. No one would accept that. Yep, that's effectively what is happening with AI today.",
