      "fragment_index": 6,
      "start": 293.98,
      "end": 349.57,
      "duration": 55.59,
      "text": "One way forward is better language annotations. Our language annotations project is one way we're working on this. This initiative, which is hosted on ML Commons Dinerbench, aims to gather annotations for languages other than English. Another of our initiatives is our web languages project on GitHub, through which we gather URLs in as many languages as possible, which we then add to our seed crawl. The aim of these initiatives is to strengthen and celebrate language, community and culture. We need richer metadata, so researchers and developers know exactly what's in the dataset they're using. That transparency helps us spot gaps, improve representation, and helps model builders build safer multilingual systems. Without clarity on what's inside the data, we can't hope to fix",
