      "text": "the problems downstream in the models. At the WMDQS or WIMDUX workshop at the column conference later this year in Montreal, and at similar forums, we're starting to see a global community form around these issues. People are realizing that data infrastructure is just as important as model architecture. It's not enough to scale compute and tweak parameters. We also need to invest in the pipelines, standards and transparency to keep AI safe and trustworthy. Open innovation depends on open foundations. The open source definition from the open source initiative has given us clear rules for software licensing. Rules that unlocked an entire ecosystem. We need something similar for AI data. Most datasets today don't come with those guarantees. Without open data, models aren't",
