      "text": "truly open, and source code alone doesn't cut it. If you can't see the data, you can't reproduce the results, and you can't build real trust. There's also important work happening in signaling. Creative Commons has proposed CC signals, a way for creators to say how their work should or shouldn't be used in AI training. At the same time, working groups at the IETF are drafting standards for how websites can communicate with crawlers and automated agents. Beyond copyright debates, groups like OpenFuture argue that we should view generative AI as a cultural and social technology, one that changes how societies value and share knowledge. The point is that this isn't just a technical problem, it's a societal one. In conclusion, openness is more than access.",
