      "duration": 65.46,
      "text": "True openness requires licensing clarity, public infrastructure and shared standards, not just public URLs. Web scale data sets deserve web scale governance. We need common protocols for signaling, attribution and responsible reuse, like those emerging at Creative Commons and the IETF. We're building trust at the infrastructure layer, from licensing to language representation, common crawl enables transparency that model cards alone cannot provide. Openness must include everyone. If AI is to serve a global public, our data practices must reflect global voices, not just dominant languages or institutions. Open data is not a side issue, it's the foundation of AI. Without open transparent reproducible data, we cannot have open models. If we want AI that is safe, multilingual and genuinely innovative, we need to treat data infrastructure with the same",
